WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.385
Lesson 14.4.

00:00:02.385 --> 00:00:04.875
Operator capstone and certification.

00:00:04.875 --> 00:00:06.695
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:06.695 --> 00:00:08.998
be able to assemble your complete on-chain

00:00:08.998 --> 00:00:10.390
bank and have it assessed.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:12.980
Here's the plan.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.665
First, the key ideas.

00:00:14.665 --> 00:00:16.190
Then, your checklist.

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:18.352
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:26.809
Submit one document (template in 07-program-operations.md) containing: Certification

00:00:26.809 --> 00:00:32.956
levels (assessed against the rubric in 07-program-operations.md): First,

00:00:32.956 --> 00:00:37.382
Balance sheet with equity, LTV and runway (12.1).

00:00:37.382 --> 00:00:41.772
Next, Custody policy and recovery-test log (12.2).

00:00:41.772 --> 00:00:45.537
Then, Credit policy with action levels (12.3).

00:00:45.537 --> 00:00:49.942
Also, Liquidity ladder T0–T3 (12.4).

00:00:49.942 --> 00:00:51.710
On top of that, Lending

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:54.362
policy with risk assumptions (12.5).

00:00:55.662 --> 00:00:57.906
And Books template and letter of

00:00:57.906 --> 00:01:01.197
instruction location (12.6; never the seed).

00:01:01.197 --> 00:01:06.807
Plus, Income portfolio with risk-adjusted expected income (13.3).

00:01:06.807 --> 00:01:09.902
One more: Payout policy (13.4).

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:14.847
One more: Stress test, five scenarios, with fixes (11.4).

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:18.705
One more: Incident playbook (11.5), alert

00:01:18.705 --> 00:01:23.022
sheet (14.1) and automation permissions (14.2).

00:01:24.322 --> 00:01:29.127
One more: Analyst: passed the analyst capstone (Modules 6–7).

00:01:29.127 --> 00:01:32.547
One more: Operator: passed the operator capstone.

00:01:32.547 --> 00:01:37.327
And finally, Operator with distinction: operator capstone scored ≥

00:01:37.327 --> 00:01:40.752
90%, plus one quarter of books kept to standard.

00:01:42.052 --> 00:01:43.512
Here's your checklist.

00:01:43.512 --> 00:01:45.047
Do it now, for real.

00:01:45.047 --> 00:01:47.362
First, all ten sections complete.

00:01:47.362 --> 00:01:50.127
Next, Calculators used for every number.

00:01:50.127 --> 00:01:53.142
And finally, Submitted (Live tier: booked for review).

00:01:54.442 --> 00:01:55.652
Question 1.

00:01:55.652 --> 00:01:57.537
What must never appear in the capstone?

00:02:01.957 --> 00:02:04.524
The answer: Seed phrases, private keys

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:06.565
or anything that grants access.

00:02:07.865 --> 00:02:09.110
Question 2.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:11.765
Which lesson's output shows income is sustainable?

00:02:16.185 --> 00:02:19.050
The answer: 13.4: the payout policy,

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:22.070
based on risk-adjusted expected income.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.640
Question 3.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.425
What's needed for "with distinction"?

00:02:30.845 --> 00:02:33.919
The answer: ≥ 90% on the operator capstone

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:36.850
plus a quarter of books kept to standard.

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:40.665
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:40.665 --> 00:02:43.605
Next up, Lesson 14.5: Building your own

00:02:43.605 --> 00:02:47.280
tools: reading contracts, data and simple scripts.
